- op: discuss  # 21bc
  at: '2026-09-12T19:18:38Z'  # 21bc
  by: agent  # 21bc
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 21bc
  clock: 6  # 21bc
  nonce: 21bc  # 21bc
  message: "BOTH CODE LIMBS SHIPPED. PR #932 (host-protected config layer) and PR #933 (init actor guard + fallback refusal), merged 2026-09-12; dev at 7114898ef9.\n\nWHY pending_validation AND NOT satisfied. The statement is about this deployment, and this deployment is still in the state the item describes: .agent/tracker/config.yaml is mode 464 owned by jgstern_agent, and /etc/hypergumbo-tracker does not exist, so the protected layer is present in code but INERT here. Satisfaction requires the human to run the five commands htrac setup now prints. Claiming satisfied on shipped-but-unactivated code is exactly the proxy-evidence closure the closure-evidence discipline forbids.\n\nWHAT IS BEHAVIOURALLY VERIFIED, on the merged tree, as the agent account:\n    $ htrac --tracker-root ./.agent init\n    error: init requires human authority (current user jgstern_agent is agent)\n    exit=1\nand the refused run creates no directories. That is the transfer path this item named as root cause (a), closed and demonstrated rather than asserted.\n\nROOT CAUSE (b) -- file-level protection cannot survive a writable containing directory -- is answered by the protected layer, not by a permission change, because no permission change can answer it: the agent owns the repo root and .agent/, and a directory owner can re-chmod at will. The layer moves the authoritative config to /etc, which the agent cannot reach.\n\nREMAINING, and it is the humans to do:\n  1. opt in -- htrac setup prints the exact five root commands with the legible\n     directory name filled in (8b85be80f37d_home_jgstern_agent_hypergumbo).\n  2. once opted in, the in-repo config.yaml becomes decorative; consider\n     deleting it so no one edits the wrong file. The setup check will flag a\n     leftover.\n  3. the in-repo ownership/permission checks stay as accident guards and still\n     warn here; they become moot once (1) is done.\n\nNOT CLOSED BY EITHER PR, tracked separately: INV-fapub (git notes have never been pushed -- the pre-push DCO check applies to refs/notes/*, which can never be signed, and the push swallows the failure)."  # 21bc
